I'd tend to agree; a permanent light source can be _very_ useful,
especially if you rely on ranged attacks a lot and if the RNG is
stingy with oil and charging (my current game so far: one magic lamp,
one non-magic lamp, one potion of oil, no scrolls of charging).

It's still a good idea to bless the lamp, so that you can rub it for a
wish if you ever decide you need one more than you need lighting.
Carrying one unused wish around has its own advantages anyway.

